Joining a domain
================

From the desktop:

    Open "Join a Domain" from the applications menu. It asks for the domain,
    an administrator account and its password.

From a terminal:

    sudo odm-client-install --domain corp.example.internal --admin-user Administrator

Either needs root: joining writes /etc/krb5.conf, /etc/sssd/sssd.conf and the
machine's keytab, and installs the policy agent as a system service.

Leaving again:

    sudo odm-client-install --leave --domain corp.example.internal \
        --admin-user Administrator

Removing the computer account from the directory needs a domain credential.
Disconnecting this machine alone needs only root here, with --force.
